      "node_id": "kg_doc_7",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Huell Burnley Howser (October 18, 1945 – January 7, 2013) was an American television personality, actor, producer, writer, singer, and voice artist, best known for hosting, producing, and writing \"California's Gold\", his human interest show produced by KCET in Los Angeles for California PBS stations. The archive of his video chronicles offers an enhanced understanding of the history, culture, and people of California. He also voiced the Backson in \"Winnie the Pooh\" (2011).",
